    "goal": "Make the stall verdict in reckon/crew/recovery.py measure a run's quiet time from the later of its last stream record and its current attempt's start, so a run resumed or redispatched by crew resume or crew redispatch does not inherit its previous attempt's silence. Today _run_stream_quiet_seconds (used near line 4717, where the detail 'stream quiet for Ns' is built) reads only the stream, so at 17:13:26 on 2026-09-25 run r-20260925T140712076451-lane-readers-share-the-gate-aware-headroom read stalled with 'stream quiet for 1919s' 27 seconds after a resume started a new attempt whose log was 1 second old. Every attempt now records attempt_started_at (landed with every-attempt-is-supervised at 6cfbe2c7). Read it from the pointer or the current attempt record, whichever the supervisor writes, and never let quiet time exceed now minus attempt start.",
